+§4.7, §6.1 step 1 (`poisoned`) and step 2, the last row of §7. A `FileError` becomes a `failed`
+marker; the `POISON_AFTER`th becomes `poisoned`, and poisoned files are skipped unopened. Any other
+exception rolls back the file and propagates.
